    <div class="story-stage">
      <article class="story-scene is-active" data-story-scene="0" data-clock="8:04 AM">
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number">01 · SIGNAL</span><h2>A Shopify sale enters the operation.</h2><p>StockChief creates the Sales Order once, commits the exact variants and updates availability. The customer, requested date and payment condition stay attached.</p><div class="scene-proof"><span>Source event <b>shopify/orders/create</b></span><span>Duplicate protection <b>active</b></span></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui order-receipt"><div class="scene-ui__bar"><span>New Sales Order</span><b>SO-2088</b></div><div class="order-customer"><span>NP</span><div><small>CUSTOMER</small><b>North &amp; Pine</b><p>Requested Friday · Deposit required</p></div><i>Shopify</i></div><div class="order-items"><p><span>Black Tee · Small</span><b>4 × $180</b></p><p><span>Field Jacket · Medium</span><b>2 × $390</b></p></div><div class="order-total"><span>Total</span><strong>$1,500</strong></div><div class="ui-confirm"><i>✓</i> Inventory committed · availability current</div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-scene" data-story-scene="1" data-clock="8:07 AM" hidden>
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number">02 · NOTICE</span><h2>The sale creates a future shortage—not an emergency today.</h2><p>StockChief compares available stock, open orders, incoming POs, recent demand and supplier lead time. It notices Black / Small will run out four days before replenishment could normally arrive.</p><div class="scene-proof"><span>Available <b>13 units</b></span><span>Demand <b>3.8/day</b></span><span>Supplier lead time <b>12 days</b></span></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui risk-graph"><div class="scene-ui__bar"><span>Black Tee / Small</span><b class="risk-pill">Risk in 8 days</b></div><div class="graph-labels"><span>31 on hand</span><span>18 committed</span><span>13 available</span></div><svg viewBox="0 0 520 245" role="img" aria-label="Projected inventory drops below zero before incoming supply"><defs><linearGradient id="area" x1="0" x2="0" y1="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#6b5ce7" stop-opacity=".35"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#6b5ce7" stop-opacity="0"/></linearGradient></defs><path class="grid" d="M30 45H500M30 105H500M30 165H500M30 225H500"/><path class="area" d="M30 72 C120 82 140 105 205 125 S300 174 355 205 L355 225 L30 225Z"/><path class="line" d="M30 72 C120 82 140 105 205 125 S300 174 355 205 S430 225 500 235"/><path class="zero" d="M30 205H500"/><circle cx="355" cy="205" r="7"/><text x="315" y="190">Stockout</text><path class="incoming" d="M420 226V91"/><text x="390" y="76">Normal PO arrival</text></svg><div class="graph-note"><i>!</i><span><b>Promise at risk</b> Replenishment arrives after projected stockout.</span></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-scene" data-story-scene="2" data-clock="8:08 AM" hidden>
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number">03 · DECIDE</span><h2>StockChief checks the network before buying.</h2><p>Brooklyn has excess inventory. Moving 12 units is faster and cheaper; purchasing 24 more covers the remainder while respecting the supplier's case pack.</p><div class="scene-proof"><span>Decision evidence <b>6 business facts</b></span><span>Case pack <b>12 units</b></span></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui decision-board"><div class="scene-ui__bar"><span>Replenishment decision</span><b>Recommended</b></div><div class="decision-route"><article><small>BROOKLYN</small><strong>42</strong><span>12 excess</span></article><i>→</i><article><small>MONROE</small><strong>13</strong><span>short in 8 days</span></article></div><div class="decision-options"><p class="is-picked"><i>✓</i><span><b>Transfer 12 units</b><small>Arrives tomorrow · $28 internal cost</small></span><strong>Best first move</strong></p><p class="is-picked"><i>✓</i><span><b>Buy 24 units</b><small>2 case packs · expected Thursday</small></span><strong>Covers remainder</strong></p><p><i>×</i><span><b>Buy all 36 units</b><small>More cash and slower coverage</small></span><strong>Rejected</strong></p></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-scene" data-story-scene="3" data-clock="8:09 AM" hidden>
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number">04 · PREPARE &amp; ACT</span><h2>The routine work is prepared and handled within authority.</h2><p>The transfer is inside the approved unit limit. The consolidated PO is below the weekly supplier limit. Both actions retain the evidence and policy that permitted them.</p><div class="authority-callout"><span>Authority used</span><b>Usual supplier · up to $2,500/week</b><i>Approved policy</i></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui action-stack"><div class="action-card"><span class="action-card__icon">⇄</span><div><small>TRANSFER TR-1041</small><b>12 × Black Tee / Small</b><p>Brooklyn → Monroe</p></div><strong>Dispatched</strong></div><div class="action-card"><span class="action-card__icon">PO</span><div><small>PURCHASE ORDER PO-1054</small><b>24 × Black Tee / Small</b><p>ABC Apparel · $336.00</p></div><strong>Sent</strong></div><div class="action-audit"><i>✓</i><span><b>Execution verified</b><small>One transfer · one supplier message · no duplicate effects</small></span></div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-scene" data-story-scene="4" data-clock="9:16 AM" hidden>
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number">05 · UNDERSTAND</span><h2>The supplier reply becomes business state.</h2><p>StockChief connects the email to PO-1054, extracts the confirmed quantity and ETA, and recognizes that the price changed. The email itself grants no authority.</p><div class="scene-proof"><span>Matched by <b>sender + PO reference</b></span><span>Incoming ETA <b>updated</b></span></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui mail-understanding"><div class="mail-head"><span>AA</span><div><b>ABC Apparel</b><small>Re: PO-1054 confirmation</small></div><time>9:16 AM</time></div><p>Hi — we can ship all 24 units Thursday. Please note the new unit cost is <mark>$14.98</mark>. Let us know if that works.</p><div class="extraction-grid"><span><small>QUANTITY</small><b>24 confirmed</b></span><span><small>EXPECTED</small><b>Thursday</b></span><span><small>UNIT COST</small><b>$14.98</b></span></div><div class="ui-confirm"><i>✓</i> PO and incoming inventory updated</div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-scene" id="exception" data-story-scene="5" data-clock="9:17 AM" hidden>
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number scene-number--amber">06 · NEEDS YOU</span><h2>One decision deserves the owner's attention.</h2><p>The new price is 7% above the last accepted cost and exceeds the 5% automatic tolerance. StockChief calculates the consequence and stops before accepting it.</p><div class="scene-proof"><span>PO impact <b>+$23.52</b></span><span>Margin after change <b>51.2%</b></span></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui exception-card"><span class="exception-card__label">Decision by Friday</span><h3>Approve ABC Apparel's price increase?</h3><p>The order remains profitable, but the change is outside your policy.</p><div class="exception-comparison"><span><small>Previous</small><b>$14.00</b></span><i>→</i><span><small>New</small><b>$14.98</b></span><span><small>Your limit</small><b>5%</b></span></div><div class="pub-actions"><button class="pub-btn" type="button" data-demo-decision="approve">Approve this PO</button><button class="pub-btn pub-btn--secondary" type="button" data-demo-decision="ask">Ask supplier</button></div><p class="demo-result" data-demo-result hidden></p></div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-scene" data-story-scene="6" data-clock="11:20 AM" hidden>
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number">07 · VERIFY</span><h2>The physical receipt—not the invoice—changes inventory.</h2><p>The transfer and supplier delivery are received with evidence. Commitments are re-evaluated, while the supplier invoice creates the payable without receiving the goods a second time.</p><div class="scene-proof"><span>Inventory movement <b>+36</b></span><span>Duplicate receipt guard <b>active</b></span></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui receiving-card"><div class="scene-ui__bar"><span>Receive PO-1054</span><b>Complete</b></div><div class="scan-row"><span class="scan-icon">⌗</span><div><small>SCANNED</small><b>BLACK-S · Lot 26-09-B</b></div><strong>24</strong></div><div class="receipt-ledger"><p><span>Physical receipt</span><b>On hand +24</b></p><p><span>Supplier invoice</span><b>Payable +$359.52</b></p><p><span>Inventory duplicate</span><b class="muted">None</b></p></div><div class="ui-confirm"><i>✓</i> Receipt, PO and accounting evidence linked</div></div>
      </article>
      <article class="story-scene" data-story-scene="7" data-clock="3:32 PM" hidden>
        <div class="scene-copy"><span class="scene-number">08 · COMPLETE</span><h2>The customer order leaves with its full story intact.</h2><p>Inventory is issued at physical handoff, tracking is attached, the remaining payment is recorded, and accounting posts revenue and COGS exactly once.</p><div class="scene-proof"><span>Promised arrival <b>Friday</b></span><span>Order balance <b>$0</b></span></div></div>
        <div class="scene-ui fulfillment-card"><div class="shipment-label"><div><small>SHIP TO</small><b>North &amp; Pine</b><span>48 Mercer Street · Brooklyn, NY</span></div><strong>UPS</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 200 45" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 2v40M12 2v40M18 2v40M31 2v40M38 2v40M51 2v40M57 2v40M69 2v40M76 2v40M82 2v40M95 2v40M108 2v40M114 2v40M127 2v40M133 2v40M146 2v40M154 2v40M166 2v40M180 2v40M193 2v40"/></svg><span>1Z84X20Y0392018382</span></div><div class="fulfillment-events"><p><i>✓</i><span><b>Inventory issued</b><small>6 items · Monroe</small></span></p><p><i>✓</i><span><b>Payment completed</b><small>$1,000 final balance</small></span></p><p><i>✓</i><span><b>Books updated</b><small>Revenue and COGS linked</small></span></p></div></div>
